INT. RUINED CHURCH BELL TOWER - DAWN

Stone stairs wind up into broken light. The bell lies cracked on its side, green with age. Through a hole in the wall, smoke rises from a distant town.

SERGEANT REYNALDO CASTELLANOS-DUBE (40s, scarf over his mouth, rifle across his shoulders) crouches at the arched window. PRIVATE OSKAR LINDGREN-PARK (19, glasses taped at the bridge) hugs the radio set. CORPORAL ABIOLA FAGBENLE (30s, sniper's cheekrest slung on her back) scans the tree line with binoculars. PRIVATE TEMUJIN BATBAYAR (20s, silent, chewing on a stalk of grass) stacks sandbags. LIEUTENANT HONORIA WEXCOMBE (30s, mud to her thighs, helmet cocked back) looks over a map weighted with a rock.

                    WEXCOMBE
          Report.

                    FAGBENLE
          Two vehicles, north road. Neither moving.

                    CASTELLANOS-DUBE
          Waiting for us to blink.

                    WEXCOMBE
          Then we don't blink. Lindgren-Park, raise HQ.

                    LINDGREN-PARK
          Yes, ma'am.

He turns the dial. Static washes. A voice rises out of it, distorted.

                    STERNBERG (V.O.)
                (radio)
          Echo Three, this is Command. Say your status.

                    WEXCOMBE
          Command, Echo Three. Tower held. Two hostile vehicles on the north road.

                    STERNBERG (V.O.)
                (radio)
          Copy. Armor is thirty minutes out. Hold position.

                    WEXCOMBE
          Thirty minutes is a long time.

                    STERNBERG (V.O.)
                (radio)
          It's what we have.

Batbayar stops stacking. Cocks his head.

                    BATBAYAR
          Engines.

Everyone listens. Faint, then louder. A low mechanical growl rolls up the valley.

                    FAGBENLE
          They're moving. Both.

                    CASTELLANOS-DUBE
          Positions.

The team scatters. Fagbenle drops prone behind the window, rifle out. Batbayar drags sandbags to the stairwell mouth. Castellanos-Dube takes the opposite window. Lindgren-Park curls around the radio, mouth against the handset.

                    LINDGREN-PARK
          Command, Command, contact imminent.

                    STERNBERG (V.O.)
                (radio, breaking up)
          ...say again...

                    WEXCOMBE
          Make it brief.

                    LINDGREN-PARK
          Contact.

The first shell whistles. The tower shudders. Dust pours from the ceiling. The cracked bell rings once, a bruised, enormous note.
